## Migration

Replaced by:

- `harness/tool-call-review`: Explore decision-based tool appropriateness review
- `harness/intent-drift`: Explore review for drift from user intent
- `harness/edit-summaries`: Report per-edit diff and line-count summaries
- `harness/change-reasons`: Explore required reasons for code mutations
- `harness/review-gates`: Choose a minimal workflow for entry and exit review gates
- `harness/model-council`: Consult several models and synthesize their responses
- `harness/config-assistant`: Open a dedicated assistant for Shellfish configuration
- `harness/temporary-sessions`: Explore temporary sessions for incognito use
- `research/agent-survey`: Survey agent projects for concrete Shellfish improvements
- `research/self-improvement`: Explore self-modifying skills, memory, and scripts with rewind
- `research/context-editing`: Evaluate selective context editing

Alternative gate designs are retained as options in harness/review-gates rather than independent implementation commitments. The existing sandbox approver already has risk, authorization, and untrusted-instruction dimensions. Any further policy changes can be investigated separately if needed.
